      "path": "README.md",
      "content": "# Pixel Two-Number Calculator\n\nA self-contained, offline pixel-style calculator built with plain HTML, CSS, and JavaScript. No packages, no network requests, no storage.\n\n## Features\n\n- Add, subtract, multiply, divide two numbers\n- Supports negative and decimal inputs\n- Rejects empty, non-finite (NaN/Infinity), and division-by-zero cases with the exact text `Error`\n- Output shows only the numeric result (initial value `0`)\n- Pixel/retro theme with hover, focus, and pressed states\n- Fully keyboard accessible with visible focus outlines\n- Responsive layout down to 360px wide\n\n## Usage\n\n1. Open `index.html` in any modern browser.\n2. Enter a number in **Left Number** and **Right Number**.\n3. Choose an operation from the dropdown.\n4. Click **Calculate** (or press Enter in an input field).\n5. The result appears in the output box; errors display `Error`.\n\n## Keyboard Accessibility\n\n- Tab moves through all labeled controls\n- Enter in either number input triggers calculation\n- Visible focus ring on all interactive elements\n\n## Constraints Met\n\n- Only `index.html` and `README.md`\n- No external assets, imports, packages, or server code\n- `addEventListener` used exclusively (no inline handlers)\n- Required IDs preserved: `left`, `right`, `operation`, `calculate`, `result`\n- Result output contains only the number or `Error` (no labels)\n- Under 200 lines total\n\n## Manual Test Checklist\n\n- [ ] Empty left or right → `Error`\n- [ ] Non-numeric input → `Error`\n- [ ] Division by zero → `Error`\n- [ ] Negative numbers calculate correctly\n- [ ] All four operations produce correct results\n- [ ] Initial result is `0`\n- [ ] Layout works at 360px width\n- [ ] Keyboard navigation and focus states visible\n- [ ] No network requests in DevTools",
